Q: CSS counter-reset inside sibling div doesn&#39;t work A: <p>If you want two independent list counters you could use two independent list counters. Like so:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.list-ol1 {
  counter-reset: itm1;
  list-style-type: none;
}

.list-ol1 .item {
  counter-increment: itm1;
}

.list-ol1 .item::before {
  content: counters(itm1, ".") ". ";
}

.list-ol2 {
  counter-reset: itm2;
  list-style-type: none;
}

.list-ol2 .item {
  counter-increment: itm2;
}

.list-ol2 .item::before {
  content: counters(itm2, ".") ". ";
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>List 1
&lt;ol class="list-ol1"&gt;
  &lt;li class="item"&gt;Item 1&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li class="item"&gt;Item 2&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li class="item"&gt;Item 3 
    &lt;ol class="list-ol1"&gt;
      &lt;li class="item"&gt;item 3.1&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ol&gt;
  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div&gt;
  List 2
  &lt;ol class="list-ol2"&gt;
    &lt;li class="item"&gt;Item 1&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li class="item"&gt;Item 2
      &lt;ol class="list-ol2"&gt;
        &lt;li class="item"&gt;item 2.1&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;/ol&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>You only need a separate class, or id, for the counter properties. All other CSS properties of the lists could be placed in a common class.</p>

Q: How to zoom an ImageView when click a button in android A: <p>Try this code for Zoom in and Zoom out of ImageView,</p>

<p>Put this in  main.xml :</p>

<pre><code>&lt;ZoomControls
        android:id="@+id/zoomControls1"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_alignParentBottom="true"
        android:layout_centerHorizontal="true"
        android:layout_marginBottom="40dp" /&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>In MainActivity.java :</p>

<pre><code> zoom = (ZoomControls) findViewById(R.id.zoomControls1);
     zoom.setOnZoomInClickListener(new OnClickListener() {

            @Override
            public void onClick(View v) {
                // TODO Auto-generated method stub

                float x = img.getScaleX();
                float y = img.getScaleY();

                img.setScaleX((float) (x+1));
                img.setScaleY((float) (y+1));
            }
        });

            zoom.setOnZoomOutClickListener(new View.OnClickListener() {

            @Override
            public void onClick(View v) {
                // TODO Auto-generated method stub


                float x = img.getScaleX();
                float y = img.getScaleY();

                img.setScaleX((float) (x-1));
                img.setScaleY((float) (y-1));
            }
        });
</code></pre>

<p>I wish it will help you..</p>

